  "Textbook. Let me tell you about textbook. In ’83, a boy sat there — your seat, Dee — bid seven holding four and a prayer. Whole shop stopped cutting. You know why I remember? Because June here took the book that set him, without looking up from her magazine.": [
   728865,
   12960
  ],
  "And Dee — your friend Ray sent word the porch is standing. Porches fall, baby. Shops too. Show me the route ain’t just talk.": [
   742075,
   6270
  ],
  "Ray’s porch first, then my shop. That’s the right order. That’s how it was always done.": [
   748595,
   5590
  ],
  "Same chairs, same rules. Ace Down. But I noticed something last time — you play like you’re apologizing. In this shop we don’t apologize to cards.": [
   754435,
   6795
  ],
  "Clean. Correct. Every book accounted for… You play like you were raised by people who read.": [
   761480,
   7425
  ],
  "The Rec Center is next, Lord help you. Two boys over there play loud and fast and think noise is a strategy.": [
   769155,
   5640
  ],
  "And when you pass the shop window coming back — knock. Winners in this classroom always report back.": [
   775045,
   5185
  ],
  "No shame in it. Everybody loses in this chair before they win in it. I did. In ’79. June still brings it up at holidays.": [
   780480,
   9185
  ],
  "Last time you bid your hopes. I’ve thought about it during three haircuts. Today we see if the lesson took root or just took notes.": [
   789915,
   6610
  ],
  "Again. In my chair. A student who keeps returning stops being a student, June. What do we call them?": [
   796775,
   5615
  ],
  "…June. She’s READING me. In my own shop. …Deal. Before she reads the wallpaper too.": [
   802640,
   5040
  ],
  "The graduates return. Sit — no lesson today. Today you’re colleagues, and colleagues get the hard game with no teaching discount.": [
   807930,
   8495
  ],
  "Then defend it like you were raised right. Ace Down.": [
   816675,
   4500
  ],
  "Habits are just history that hasn’t introduced itself yet.": [
   821425,
   3560
  ],
  "Hmm. The students are ahead in my classroom. June, note the date.": [
   825235,
   5325
  ],
  "The book is patient. The book has been patient since before your street had a name.": [
   830810,
   5185
  ],
  "In ’83 courage and arithmetic looked exactly alike until the last trick.": [
   836245,
   5230
  ],
  "Match point in my shop. The clippers stop for this. Forty years, and the room still knows when it’s real.": [
   841725,
   7805
  ],
  "Play it like you studied. That’s all anybody here ever asked.": [
   849780,
   3890
  ],
  "I wrote the footnotes. Play on.": [
   853920,
   2725
  ],
  "The book, chapter four: a lost hand is tuition. What matters is whether you attend the lesson.": [
   856895,
   6910
  ],
  "Second lesson, first hand. The book opens where the bookmark was. Show me the bookmark moved.": [
   864055,
   6130
  ],
  "A big bid in a no-joker shop. The book calls that \"conviction.\" The book also has a chapter on what conviction costs.": [
   870435,
   6825
  ],
  "A clean cut. Chapter nine: \"the spade is patient.\" I didn’t write that chapter, but I assign it.": [
   877510,
   6750
  ],
  "A game with a swing like the one we saw is a game that teaches twice. Pay attention to which lesson is yours.": [
   884510,
   6320
  ],
  "The face-down one is mine to know. A barber keeps some cuts private. Play well and I might tell it standing over your chair in thirty years.": [
   891080,
   8530
  ],
  "Whatever happens now — it gets told right. We’re all here to tell it.": [
   899860,
   4085
  ],
  "Ray’s in the tall chair — Thursday regular. Don’t mind him. He grades every bid like report cards came home.": [
   904195,
   6505
  ],
  "Because she’s about to teach, Raymond. Hush now — class is in session.": [
   910950,
   3515
  ],
  "Frederick Douglass. Taught himself to read when it was forbidden to him, escaped slavery at twenty, and wrote it all down for the world to answer for.": [
   914715,
   8230
  ],
  "Harriet Tubman. She got herself free — then went back some thirteen times for family and strangers alike, and she brought out every single one.": [
   923195,
   8920
  ],
  "Nat Turner. In 1831 he rose in Southampton County and led the deadliest slave rebellion in American history.": [
   932365,
   6565
  ],
  "Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Twenty-six years old when Montgomery stopped riding the buses — and he led that boycott all 381 days.": [
   939180,
   7365
  ],
  "Sojourner Truth. Born enslaved — and the first Black woman to win a court case against a white man in this country, bringing her own son home.": [
   946795,
   6635
  ],
  "Fannie Lou Hamer. A Mississippi sharecropper who stood before a national convention in 1964 and told the truth until the whole country had to listen.": [
   953680,
   9700
  ],
  "Marcus Garvey. He built the largest Black movement of his age — and put our own ships on the water with the Black Star Line.": [
   963630,
   7010
  ],
  "Ida B. Wells. A mob wrecked her newspaper office for printing the truth about lynching — so she carried that truth north and printed it louder.": [
   970890,
   8440
  ],
  "W.E.B. Du Bois. The first Black man to earn a Ph.D. from Harvard, in 1895 — and he spent ninety-five years writing the record straight.": [
   979580,
   8160
  ],
  "Malcolm X. He remade himself in a prison cell — walked out teaching discipline, dignity, and standing up straight.": [
   987990,
   7820
  ],
  "Angela Davis. A philosopher they put on trial in 1972 — she walked out acquitted, and she has been teaching ever since.": [
   996060,
   8335
  ],
  "Huey P. Newton. In 1966, in Oakland, he co-founded the Black Panther Party — and a neighborhood's protection became a movement.": [
   1004645,
   8315
  ],
  "Hold on now. That's Malcolm they just cut. The man told us freedom would come 'by any means necessary' — a spade on a playing card changes none of it.": [
   1013210,
   8275
  ],
  "Malcolm X, cut down on a trick. He taught a whole generation to stand up straight — 'by any means necessary' was never a slogan. It was a promise.": [
   1021735,
   8950
  ],
